# Built APK served from /download — a 31 MB regenerable build artifact.
# Committing it would bloat this PUBLIC repo permanently; it is deployed
# straight to the host by scripts/deploy_app.sh instead.
app/download/*.apk

# Play listing screenshots — regenerable via scripts/play_screenshots.mjs
app/play-shots/

# iOS listing screenshots — regenerable via scripts/ios_screenshots.mjs
app/ios-shots/

# Register manifest signing key (private half lives in ~/hawkeye-secrets)
register-signing.key

# --- Election audits -------------------------------------------------------
# The evidence, not the method. Sheets are INEC's published EC8A scans (1.3 GB
# for Osun alone) and the JSONL runs are model output regenerable from them —
# committing either would bloat this PUBLIC repo permanently for no gain. The
# scripts, the README and each race's RACE.md ARE tracked: those are the audit
# method, which is the part that has to be inspectable.
audits/*/sheets/
audits/*/crop_preview/
audits/*/*.jsonl
audits/*/*.jsonl.*
audits/*/*.xlsx
audits/*/*.log

# Derived work queues. Every one is regenerated by stage1_triage.mjs or
# stage0_*.mjs from the run files, changes on each re-run, and is worthless as
# history — tier_c.json alone is 283 KB of file names. What IS kept below is the
# human work (hand_labels), the durable claim (no-sheet) and the deliverable
# (findings), which together are under 35 KB.
audits/*/tier_*.json
audits/*/stage0_targets.json
audits/*/stage0_reread.json
audits/*/party_targets.json
audits/*/row_integrity.json
audits/*/labelled_20.json

# Rented-GPU pod connection details. Holds the pod's Jupyter access token, which
# is not an account credential but is still a live key to a running machine, and
# this repo is public.
backend/scripts/pod_env.sh

# iOS signing material. credentials.json holds the .p12 password in clear text
# (EAS defines the format), and this repo is public.
credentials.json
native/credentials.json
*.p12
*.mobileprovision
*.p8
*.certSigningRequest
